 "Hi! I'm Nebula, the expedition's pilot cat. First stop: the Moon. Soon the Sun sets and the panels produce nothing. How will you keep the air running until dawn? Hint: count how much energy your base uses per day and multiply it by the nights.": "0ecaab4f34f2.mp3",
 "You made it to dawn! Whatever you saved carries over as a reserve to the next mission. This is how NASA thinks when it designs the Fission Surface Power reactor.": "f945fcd8e545.mp3",
 "Air needs energy: oxygen is made by splitting water. And recovering water costs energy too. Here the Sun doesn't set for the whole mission. Watch the mass bar: every kilo you put on the rocket counts. The recycler is heavy, but it recovers almost all the water.": "89e752a2b3d8.mp3",
 "Mission complete! Now we travel to Mars. Your reserves come with you.": "0cdf287c898b.mp3",
 "We made it to Mars! New base: before you decide, check your reserves. Mars has a CO₂ atmosphere: MOXIE can turn it into oxygen without using water. Panels produce less than half of what they do on the Moon, and dust can cover them for days. More energy for the crops leaves less for later.": "7830885e1e45.mp3",
 "First harvest on Mars! This harvest stays as a reserve for the next mission.": "3cde1c942534.mp3",
 "From Mars, a signal takes between 3 and 22 minutes to arrive from Earth. If a solar alert arrives, you can't wait for an answer: you decide when to go into the shelter. Shielding protects every day, but it is heavy. The shelter protects a lot, but no science is done while inside.": "6a2b8deb43ee.mp3",
 "You protected your crew! This is how the astronauts who reach Mars will prepare.": "dae524c16c21.mp3",
 "NASA satellites watch the Sun. When they warn of a flare, you will have one day to react. Shielding protects every day, but it is heavy. The shelter protects a lot, but no science is done while inside.": "33de7b25b8a1.mp3",
 "Well done! This is how Artemis astronauts will protect themselves on the Moon.": "ceba0d9fe804.mp3",
 "Making oxygen uses water every day. Over 40 days that is a lot of water to lift on a rocket. The extractor heats the regolith to release the ice, but it is heavy and uses energy.": "05a698a7cd45.mp3",
 "You used the Moon's own resources! That is called ISRU and it is key to the Artemis program.": "8b5b3f566ce6.mp3",
 "This mission combines everything you have learned. I will not give hints during the trip. Think about the worst day: at night, with broken panels and the recycler down.": "0363f889aed2.mp3",
 "A real commander! Your base survived a chain of problems, just like in a real mission.": "4c8b3839437a.mp3",
 "A dust storm is coming: the panels will barely produce. Save energy: turn off the greenhouse.": "648ac04ebb09.mp3",
 "A solar flare! The particles arrive tomorrow. Turn on the shelter before advancing.": "726f1d908c67.mp3",
 "Each Advance moves one day forward. If a bar reaches zero, the base fails. In the Chronoscope, tap a past day to rewind.": "fa8bb0fbf0e4.mp3",
 "The Sun has set: the panels no longer produce. Only batteries and the reactor count now.": "07df2e716d33.mp3",
 "You learned how the systems of a base are connected! That is what NASA engineers do.": "c59d9a4aebdf.mp3",
 "Every failure you understand brings you closer to being a commander. Play again!": "81d100a3d70b.mp3",
 "The lunar night lasts almost 15 days. You need many batteries… or a reactor that works day and night.": "c61fcac25f4f.mp3",
 "The ISS recovers 98 % of its water. With a recycler, a long mission needs very little reserve water.": "4358041b61cb.mp3",
 "Calculate: people × days × daily food. The greenhouse makes part of the food, but uses water and energy.": "d52c092b5f57.mp3",
 "Bring more water or install the recycler: every kilo of oxygen costs 1.125 kg of water.": "f9180f1e1648.mp3",
 "Use the shelter only when needed. The greenhouse adds extra science.": "0070b1c6ca95.mp3",
 "On Mars the Sun is weak and dust can block it for days. Bring batteries to ride out the storm… or a reactor, which does not depend on the Sun.": "dc57e8a56934.mp3",
 "Use reduced rations for only a few days.": "2a0a260468ea.mp3",
 "Bring more water or install the recycler: every kilo of oxygen costs 1.125 kg of water. On Mars, MOXIE makes oxygen from the air without using water.": "6716537d89c0.mp3",
 "When there is a solar alert, turn on the shelter for the next day.": "81705a606394.mp3",
 "Bring more water or install the recycler: every kilo of oxygen costs 1.125 kg of water. Or use the extractor: it gets ice out of the lunar soil.": "d3c46bd62bc9.mp3"
